{
  "$comment": "Page contracts (docs/design/target-state.md). One entry per surface the UI inventory walks. Every rendered heading, tab, tile, column, chip, button, summary and link on a built surface must match an entry in its allow list (exact string, or a regular expression when prefixed re:). Page-level prose (outside repeaters) must fit the budget. Claude Code never edits this file: a violation is fixed by removing what violates it, or reported for review with the case. `status` is flipped to built by the prompt that builds the surface; `enforceAll` is flipped by prompt 49, after which any inventory surface without a contract fails. Controls (buttons, links, chips) inside a repeater are items and are measured under `rows`, not against the surface's allow lists. An element matching `.step-title` is reported as `title` and measured against rules.stepTitleMaxWords, never as a heading. A surface may override the row budget with `rowBudget`.",
